WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:05.975
Lab 1 runs in the machine configuration
folder, in PowerShell 7 on Windows.

3
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:09.525
Nothing signs in, uploads,
or installs the agent.

4
00:00:09.525 --> 00:00:12.892
Step one saves three pinned
modules from the PowerShell

5
00:00:12.892 --> 00:00:15.900
Gallery into a folder,
rather than installing them.

6
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:21.232
Because of that download, the results on
these slides weren't re-run for this deck:

7
00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:24.140
they're the ones Chapter
07's Lab 1 text gives,

8
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.725
as the path's verification log records.

9
00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:29.250
Step two follows Learn's steps by hand.

10
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:33.375
Compile the configuration, and
package it twice from the same MOF.

11
00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:36.163
You get two packages with
two different hashes.

12
00:00:36.163 --> 00:00:40.671
Look inside the MOF, and your user name
and computer name are in the header,

13
00:00:40.671 --> 00:00:43.376
and your folder path is
in every source info.

14
00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:48.957
Step three runs the package check on
Learn's output: two MC-PKG oh four findings,

15
00:00:48.957 --> 00:00:51.836
for build-host data and an absolute path,

16
00:00:51.836 --> 00:00:55.200
and the oh seven warning,
no version in the name.
